xl2tpd 1.3.20: make the -DTEST_HIDDEN build compile and hide the Assigned
Session ID the way encrypt_avp expects.

Dockerfile.lac builds xl2tpd with -DTEST_HIDDEN so a LAC whose section sets
`hidden bit = yes` sends AVP 14 hidden (add_callid_avp, avpsend.c), the one
AVP xl2tpd can hide. Upstream's add_callid_avp still carries `raw++` from
before the add_header refactor; `raw` is declared nowhere, so that build stops
at a compile error. encrypt_avp (aaa.c) reads the clear AVP two octets past
the hidden header it writes, so the clear AVP is written two octets in. With
hbit unset (every config but the hidden scenario's) shift stays 0 and the
AVP is the octets the unpatched code writes.

--- a/avpsend.c
+++ b/avpsend.c
@@ -175,14 +175,20 @@
 int add_callid_avp (struct buffer *buf, _u16 callid)
 {
 #endif
-    struct half_words *ptr = (struct half_words *) (buf->start + buf->len + sizeof(struct avp_hdr));
+    /* encrypt_avp (aaa.c) rewrites a clear AVP that starts two octets past
+       buf->len into its hidden form, so a hidden Assigned Session ID is
+       written there. The upstream "raw++" names no variable and does not
+       compile. */
+    int shift = 0;
 #ifdef TEST_HIDDEN
     if (t->hbit)
-        raw++;
+        shift = 2;
 #endif
+    struct half_words *ptr = (struct half_words *) (buf->start + buf->len + shift + sizeof(struct avp_hdr));
+    buf->len += shift;
     add_header(buf, 0x8, 0xE);
     ptr->s0 = htons (callid);
-    buf->len += 0x8;
+    buf->len += 0x8 - shift;
 #ifdef TEST_HIDDEN
     if (t->hbit)
         encrypt_avp (buf, 8, t);
